<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy Cross Minster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">begun c. 1315</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Heilig-Kreuz-Münster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy Cross Minster is the main church of Schwäbisch Gmünd in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its choir, begun in 1351 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-parler">Heinrich Parler</a>, is an early and influential example of the late Gothic hall church in Germany. Heinrich's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-parler">Peter Parler</a> trained there before building <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-vitus-cathedral">St Vitus Cathedral</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, spreading the Parler style across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
